    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (74.41) and **Lawrence Butler** (70.88) headline our active roster as the clear elite plays. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** draws a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a (4.42 xERA), and his position in the #3 hole provides the run-producing upside we prioritize. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** benefits immensely from a 13% boost due to dynamic platoon splits and a significant park factor, making him a high-ceiling anchor for our outfield. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) also grades out exceptionally well, as his favorable placement in the #2 spot against Jobe allows him to capitalize on a 12% platoon advantage, firmly securing his spot as our top 1B option.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Gleyber Torres** (50.33), who just barely missed the cut. While he benefits from the #1 spot in the lineup, his negative platoon split against Legumina ultimately dragged his efficiency score below our active threshold, allowing **Zack Gelof** (57.37) and **Luis Arraez** (55.44) to maintain their spots. We are also keeping a close watch on **Bryce Harper** (62.31), whose xwOBA of 0.390 suggests he could outperform his score despite a moderate matchup against Kirby. Conversely, **Braden Montgomery** remains on the bench (36.71) due to an elite-level matchup against deGrom (3.05 xERA), which suppresses his output below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" \n\nWe enter today with no major weather concerns, though managers should note that while **Yainer Diaz** (51.65), **Cal Raleigh** (49.95), and **Justin Crawford** (52.16) are cleared to start, their efficiency is slightly constrained by lower spots in their respective batting orders. We are effectively bypassing **Tyler Freeman** as he remains in the minors, and we will continue to monitor the status of **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Will Smith** to ensure our game caps are being utilized only on the highest-efficiency matchups available. We are currently leaning into speed-heavy profiles like **Justin Crawford** to keep our SB category competitive, even when his raw offensive efficiency dips near the 50-point mark.",
